  "reference_answer": "Honestly, I'd rather work from home most of the time. The main reason is the commute — I used to spend nearly two hours a day on the train, and that time now goes into sleep or a proper breakfast. I also focus better without the office chatter, so I get more done in fewer hours. That said, I wouldn't want to be fully remote. I miss the casual chats that often turn into useful ideas, and some tasks are just easier face to face. So a hybrid setup suits me best — maybe three days at home and two in the office. It gives me the quiet I need without cutting me off from people completely.",
