  "reference_answer": "Not really, and the honest reason is that I'm terrible at switching off at home. When my desk is two metres from my bed, I keep answering messages at ten at night, because there's no clear line between work and everything else. In the office, leaving the building is like a switch — I walk out and I'm done. So I'd say I prefer working from home occasionally, maybe when I need a quiet day for writing, but not as my normal setup. It's less about the work itself and more about whether I can actually stop.",
